{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_64e50074d85103060014dfd2e404f3e16bc8ddc9960953cf5e4abbb269b2dbcc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product requires Tailscale and Chrome on both machines, and the Linux sink must bind a Tailscale 100.x address, refusing to start without the tailnet."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bdbef00468a7bee0142a460ce108d9509a632462ac71580b6fcee6f34f3ba592"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On Linux, a missing blocklist.yaml or omitted policy field means the sink ships nothing (allowlist-empty) as a security default; sync-all requires an explicit blocklist policy with an empty domains list, described as an operator choice rather than the code default."}],"claim_ids":["clm_64e50074d85103060014dfd2e404f3e16bc8ddc9960953cf5e4abbb269b2dbcc","clm_bdbef00468a7bee0142a460ce108d9509a632462ac71580b6fcee6f34f3ba592"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb","id":"pg_14ce0ff9637955cc8d54e46737a1fefa","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/mvanhorn-agentcookie-docs-consumption-md-57b53dfd9162-e46737a1fefa.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_55dfcec9a5085a97866e4ed74cec5710"],"title":"mvanhorn/agentcookie/docs/consumption.md @ 57b53dfd9162","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_217080b97abe02d053cebc2bc97c0b61f0e170fc479bf358fb0fbb352db7e033"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture doc lays out Go packages including cmd/agentcookie (cobra CLI), internal/cli, internal/chrome, internal/transport, internal/config, internal/pairing, internal/keystore, internal/protocol, and internal/cdp."},{"claim_ids":["clm_64e50074d85103060014dfd2e404f3e16bc8ddc9960953cf5e4abbb269b2dbcc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product requires Tailscale and Chrome on both machines, and the Linux sink must bind a Tailscale 100.x address, refusing to start without the tailnet."},{"claim_ids":["clm_856e0652a55416bf71836e48d841e20d891b59ab0ea81d7d9fa4afa804896462"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The sync protocol carries a versioned SyncEnvelope with a monotonic Sequence; the sink rejects wrong keys with 401, version mismatches with 400, and replays via an in-memory SequenceTracker with 409."},{"claim_ids":["clm_883b948f84a528007a60465948774ffebb85547487ba73c9af168c262550a91f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On Linux the sink injects cookies directly into Chrome's in-memory store via the Chrome DevTools Protocol (Storage.setCookies) instead of rewriting Chrome's SQLite, and Chrome must be started with a remote-debugging port such as 9223."},{"claim_ids":["clm_91834bd6d42db94bc7be4e4c04a3ffd9aa54c988570999df7e25a41d21e6b36b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Cookies are sealed with AES-GCM using per-peer keys derived from an X25519 + HKDF pairing handshake in which the pairing code is mixed into the HKDF salt; key files are stored mode 0600."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bdbef00468a7bee0142a460ce108d9509a632462ac71580b6fcee6f34f3ba592"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On Linux, a missing blocklist.yaml or omitted policy field means the sink ships nothing (allowlist-empty) as a security default; sync-all requires an explicit blocklist policy with an empty domains list, described as an operator choice rather than the code default."}],"claim_ids":["clm_217080b97abe02d053cebc2bc97c0b61f0e170fc479bf358fb0fbb352db7e033","clm_64e50074d85103060014dfd2e404f3e16bc8ddc9960953cf5e4abbb269b2dbcc","clm_856e0652a55416bf71836e48d841e20d891b59ab0ea81d7d9fa4afa804896462","clm_883b948f84a528007a60465948774ffebb85547487ba73c9af168c262550a91f","clm_91834bd6d42db94bc7be4e4c04a3ffd9aa54c988570999df7e25a41d21e6b36b","clm_bdbef00468a7bee0142a460ce108d9509a632462ac71580b6fcee6f34f3ba592"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb","id":"pg_323b94f81e9159428ab1aba778d12442","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/mvanhorn-agentcookie-docs-architecture-md-57b53dfd9162-aba778d12442.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_aa0a3da2a74b5c549a74b52329b95a00"],"title":"mvanhorn/agentcookie/docs/architecture.md @ 57b53dfd9162","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3bdfe49a653f7efc4f6a54cba39d3e4fecc418e0f7d60b0923ac74172adbea4a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A recorded 2026-05-19 dry run of the closed-beta installer on a clean Mac mini concluded it was not ready for the first invite, citing blockers including broken tarball extraction, missing --code/--pair-url passthrough, and a key-file hostname mismatch that silently broke syncing."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3bdfe49a653f7efc4f6a54cba39d3e4fecc418e0f7d60b0923ac74172adbea4a"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb","id":"pg_68d4c0262274557cb42064a51cac02a6","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/mvanhorn-agentcookie-docs-dry-run-2026-05-19-md-57b53dfd9162-64a51cac02a6.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_63778faccc16571dab3447172b8e5978"],"title":"mvanhorn/agentcookie/docs/dry-run-2026-05-19.md @ 57b53dfd9162","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_64e50074d85103060014dfd2e404f3e16bc8ddc9960953cf5e4abbb269b2dbcc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product requires Tailscale and Chrome on both machines, and the Linux sink must bind a Tailscale 100.x address, refusing to start without the tailnet."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6e5b51b9f28b3198359239f7bf0607ffac6d2ad00667c36b734e911c0270ef58"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Chrome's DBSC binds Google/Workspace sessions to device keys, so copied cookies for such sites stop working within minutes; the documented workaround is signing the sink's Chrome into the same Google account locally."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7256e87791e180d626c0c934abb3abb1ec3b4dc5357f284109e1efaad611ee31"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented limits include a plaintext-at-rest sidecar at ~/.agentcookie/cookies-plain.db, a loopback-only CDP port that same-user processes can read, no live key rotation (wizard re-run required), and unread Linux extra-profile Chrome SQLite."},{"claim_ids":["clm_883b948f84a528007a60465948774ffebb85547487ba73c9af168c262550a91f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On Linux the sink injects cookies directly into Chrome's in-memory store via the Chrome DevTools Protocol (Storage.setCookies) instead of rewriting Chrome's SQLite, and Chrome must be started with a remote-debugging port such as 9223."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8d6fc2d31418ac32fc0e08e547f64d2584594935ea06f01db111b7b5f0cddc09"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the README's working-today list cites 520+ unit tests across 26 packages, a repository test-suite figure rather than any agent-performance evaluation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_91834bd6d42db94bc7be4e4c04a3ffd9aa54c988570999df7e25a41d21e6b36b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Cookies are sealed with AES-GCM using per-peer keys derived from an X25519 + HKDF pairing handshake in which the pairing code is mixed into the HKDF salt; key files are stored mode 0600."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a4ebb241bef483db16875c3200ded1bc1161a8e5fda6c40278524e8292397151"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"One source can fan out to multiple sinks, reading and filtering cookies once then sealing and POSTing to each sink with that sink's own paired key; an unreachable sink fails in isolation, and every sink receives the full cookie and secret set."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bdbef00468a7bee0142a460ce108d9509a632462ac71580b6fcee6f34f3ba592"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On Linux, a missing blocklist.yaml or omitted policy field means the sink ships nothing (allowlist-empty) as a security default; sync-all requires an explicit blocklist policy with an empty domains list, described as an operator choice rather than the code default."}],"claim_ids":["clm_64e50074d85103060014dfd2e404f3e16bc8ddc9960953cf5e4abbb269b2dbcc","clm_6e5b51b9f28b3198359239f7bf0607ffac6d2ad00667c36b734e911c0270ef58","clm_7256e87791e180d626c0c934abb3abb1ec3b4dc5357f284109e1efaad611ee31","clm_883b948f84a528007a60465948774ffebb85547487ba73c9af168c262550a91f","clm_8d6fc2d31418ac32fc0e08e547f64d2584594935ea06f01db111b7b5f0cddc09","clm_91834bd6d42db94bc7be4e4c04a3ffd9aa54c988570999df7e25a41d21e6b36b","clm_a4ebb241bef483db16875c3200ded1bc1161a8e5fda6c40278524e8292397151","clm_bdbef00468a7bee0142a460ce108d9509a632462ac71580b6fcee6f34f3ba592"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb","id":"pg_8f5381998bfc542ab3de73238e6001a4","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/mvanhorn-agentcookie-readme-md-57b53dfd9162-73238e6001a4.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_e274ec2eb4135ca694d54c11b952f1f9"],"title":"mvanhorn/agentcookie/README.md @ 57b53dfd9162","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:10:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_507b7ee63ad34e088f0d46f3ea6a9bfb"}
